			<div class="content" id="post-content-4468162">
									

<p>For the SCP-5000 contest, I have written a murder mystery. A skip is neutralised in a locked containment chamber. There's a long list of suspects. Whodunnit?</p>
<p>Fair warning - this is long, and it refers to (but does not depict) sexual abuse. I have tried to do justice to the genre, and to be fair with the information given to the audience. Let me know if I've made the clues too obscure / too obvious - I may be able to tweak this a little for future readers. Similarly, if you think the very last section doesn't belong, I'm happy to discuss removal. Spoilers in collapsibles, please!</p>
<p>A huge vote of thanks must go to Pedantique, who provided several rounds of very useful feedback on the forums. Thanks also to Kid F for their review, and to OBot321 for the vote of confidence! I also have to acknowledge my indebtedness to some of the masters of the genre - in particular Dorothy Sayers and Georgette Heyer, whose work you should really read.</p>
<p>If you like the intrepid investigator, Agent Ellen O'Connor, you may want to read about how she got her start at the Department of Analytics: <a href="/exit-interview">Exit Interview</a>.</p>
<p>I hope you enjoy this, and please don't forget to vote. Good luck everyone for the contest!</p>
<p>I can't imagine that these will be relevant, but my non-5000 preferences are:<br />
5001<br />
5999<br />
5002<br />
5003<br />
5500</p>

