<p>It's an obvious interpretation of the contest theme, sure; what is also obvious is that this is written with a clear appreciation for the genre it pays homage to, and specifically what makes this kind of fiction work in the first instance. If the writing makes me picture an old-timey swing band playing in the background as the besuited, befedoraed protagonist finger-snaps, you've done a good job of detective fiction.</p>
<p>In re: the ending, I don't particularly care for <span style="color: white">the Pataphysics reveal</span> because you know what, not every piece of genre work on the site needs a cheeky 'eh? eh? eh?' to justify its existence. I think I can suspend my disbelief and accept that this is a little ''''''unrealistic'''''' when it's this well-written already. I don't really care to have an in-universe explanation that feels somewhat like an attempt to ward off joyless nitpickers moreso than a coherent twist.</p>

