<p>Thanks very much for the feedback, Gee. I've updated those consistency points (I can't believe I missed a &quot;Ms<span style="text-decoration: underline;">.</span>&quot; after working so hard against my usual preference for all those &quot;Dr<span style="text-decoration: underline;">.</span>&quot;s).</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Agent O'Connor: This is the Foundation, doctor. Everyone has secrets.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I take your point about this line, and I wasn't absolutely confident about it. But I wanted to mix between straight segues (like &quot;do you know why he ended up as a D-Class?&quot;) and what I'd call &quot;ad-break&quot; lines to end the interviews, and this felt like the latter. If I think of something stronger, I'll use it, but I do think something a bit &quot;on the nose&quot; is needed to ensure readers open the next collapsible.</p>

